## Item A — ZoneWorld ZW-G4 (functional)
The G4 crash-boundary scenario kills the target node; the client's interrupted operation must end `Unavailable` (08-routing :322-331,
error model :75-85; the D-084/crash-boundary port af7afd28e7 implemented this) but now waits for `CrashRelocationProbeRes` and fails
"interrupted operation did not end Unavailable". Trace the operation: with the durable sender (d6ec19765e) does the interrupted
request now replay/keep waiting instead of ending Unavailable when the target generation is gone? (The sender must not retry an
operation whose target lifecycle generation disappeared — that is Unavailable by spec, not a replay case.) Or did the mesh unwind
change which terminal the join path reports? Fix at the owner; regression test in `StatefulServiceRuntimeTests`/ZoneWorld regression.

## Item B — termination outcomes
Roles exit 0 but report `ZLINK_FRAMEWORK_TERMINATION outcome=FORCE_STOPPED reason=TEARDOWN_FAILED` (TicTacToe play-b, Bingo play-a,
SupportChat support, DeliveryDispatch courier-node-1/2 + customer-gateway, GameQuest api-b) or `DEADLINE_EXCEEDED` (ShoppingMall
workflow-a). Per 05-host-relocation-flow §14 the outcome must be `Stopped/None` when teardown completes. Get the underlying
exception/cause from `ZLinkFrameworkShutdown`/host coordinator (add a temporary sink if the lifecycle logger drops it, remove
after): which owned resource fails to release — a socket/poller left by the unwind or ClientServer removal? the durable sender's
pending operation at stop? a drain that now waits on Core completion that never comes? Fix at the owner with one shutdown-order rule;
regression: a host stop test asserting Stopped/None with each channel kind active.

